      "body": "## Overview\n\nReject string stop sequences when `skip_tokenizer_init=True`. These stops need a tokenizer; accepting them silently lets generation continue without the requested stopping condition. Token-ID stops remain usable without a tokenizer.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Add the check to `SamplingParams.verify()`, alongside the other tokenizer-dependent validation.\n- Cover scalar and list stop strings, plus the tokenizer-free no-stop and token-ID cases.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe previous revision was checked with:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/pre-commit run --files vllm/sampling_params.py tests/v1/sample/test_logprobs.py tests/v1/sample/test_sampling_params.py\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/v1/sample/test_sampling_params.py -q\n```\n\nThese are historical results from the existing branch, not fresh results against today's main. The branch needs a refresh and end-to-end validation before merge; no new serving or model evaluation results are claimed.\n\n## Details\n\nThe existing guard for structured outputs already rejects tokenizer-free requests. This applies the same principle to string stops, without changing `min_tokens` or `stop_token_ids`.\n\nThis remains the original PR so its review history is preserved. A fresh search found no other PR specifically implementing this guard; broader tokenizer and token-ID validation changes address different cases. SGLang has the corresponding guard in sgl-project/sglang#27882.\n\nAI assistance was used to prepare the patch and this description.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] Used vLLM's `pr-checklist` skill for the current assessment.\n- [x] AI assistance was used.\n- [x] Design Fit: small validation change in the existing owner.\n- [ ] Testing and Validation: refresh the branch and run end-to-end validation.\n- [ ] Code Quality and Style: recheck against current main and the current documentation requirements.\n- [x] Pull Request Contents: describe the bug, scope, prior checks, and remaining validation.\n</details>",
